    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0653" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/3035: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-28T17:00:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>20. President Vasquez is considering plan for lengthening his term of office to
                    six years and Senator Alfonseca<anchor n="1" xml:id="d616-f1"/> is supporting
                    the project. As I am without instructions from the Department I shall limit my
                    action to informal representations making our attitude clear but not committing
                    us thereby to a position which we might not be able to maintain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d616-f1" n="1" xml:id="d616-f1-content">
                <p>Leader of the Partido Nacional, which united with the Partido Progresista in 1924
                    to elect President Vasquez; see <ref target="frus1924v01#pg_618"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1924, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 618</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
